\pard\s1\b\fs36 The Riverbend Community Tool Library\b0\fs24\par
\pard\s2\b\fs28 Borrowing a tool\b0\fs24\par
\pard Any resident of Riverbend can borrow up to three tools at a time. Bring a library card and a recent letter with your address on it the first time you visit.\par
\pard Most tools go out for seven days. Ladders and the tile saw go out for three, because the waiting list for them is always long.\par
\pard\s2\b\fs28 Returning a tool\b0\fs24\par
\pard Clean the tool before you bring it back, and tell the volunteer at the desk if anything is broken or missing. Nobody is charged for honest wear.\par
\pard\s2\b\fs28 Opening hours\b0\fs24\par
\pard The library opens on Tuesday and Thursday evenings and all day on Saturday. It closes for the first week of January for the annual count.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720 1.\tab Find the tool in the catalogue.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720 2.\tab Check it out at the desk.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720 3.\tab Return it on time.\par
